{"id":"meal-counts","title":"Federally paid meals: people enrolled against people fed","question":"Do the numbers San Francisco sponsors file for federally reimbursed meals in child care and adult day care hang together?","finding":"In 2024-25 San Francisco child-care and after-school sponsors reported 57,513 children enrolled but 11,147 fed on an average day, 5.2 enrolled for each one fed; the middle large county reports 2.9, and San Francisco ranks 7 of 40. Enrolment was 16,835 in 2016-17 and 126,299 in 2019-20, more than the 115,828 people under 18 then living in the city. Adult day care is consistent: sponsors claimed meals for 581 people a day, and adult day health centres separately reported about 597 attending a day.","how":"Totals are the State's published county figures for the federal Child and Adult Care Food Program, federal fiscal years 2016-17 to 2024-25: meals claimed, average daily participation, enrolment and reimbursement, by type of site. Meals per person is meals divided by average daily participation. County ranks use the three latest reports and counties with at least 1,000 daily participants (100 for adult day care).","limits":"The State publishes these numbers only as county totals: meal counts and payments for each sponsor are not public, so no organization can be tested here. The State's own notes say enrolment is not a count of distinct people; after-school sites often report the whole school roll. The jump in 2019-20 coincides with pandemic rule changes. A high ratio is a reason to ask for sponsor-level claims, not evidence about any sponsor.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"year","t":"Federal fiscal year","type":"text"},{"k":"kind","t":"Type of site","type":"text"},{"k":"sites","t":"Sites","type":"int"},{"k":"meals","t":"Meals claimed","type":"int"},{"k":"dailyPeople","t":"People fed on an average day","type":"int"},{"k":"mealsPerPerson","t":"Meals per person per year","type":"int"},{"k":"countyMedianMeals","t":"Middle large county","t